    description: "From WI-borib (docs/audits/0026; agent C, ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/borib_consumer_agreement_10302026/C_counts_disclosure.md). A recall defect found by the sweep's count comparison.\n\nThe Wolfram analyzer's own finder (find_wolfram_files / its _find_source_files override) picks up .m files, but the orchestrator's candidate pre-filter does not count .m for wolfram, so the pass is skipped as no_candidate_files and no .m file is ever analysed. Reproduced with library calls by agent C: the pre-filter skips wolfram while find_wolfram_files returns the file. The drift gate test_prefilter_candidate_set.py compares each class's file_patterns, not an overridden _find_source_files, so it cannot see this; other analyzers that override the finder are equally unguarded (not enumerated).\n\nACCEPTANCE: a .m Wolfram fixture through run_behavior_map yields Wolfram symbols; the drift gate compares the finder each analyzer actually runs; every finder override enumerated."  # 68af
    fields: {}  # 68af
